### Projection Alignment Rules (INVARIANT)
Step IDs are semantic names, not positional labels.  Use the exact `step_id`
value from the canonical projection; do not use a numeric position as an ID.

#### Compatible leaf kinds
| canonical field | compatible leaf kinds |
| --- | --- |
| action_kind `observe` | `external_precondition`, `ai_system_action`, `integration_interaction` |
| action_kind `prepare` | `external_precondition`, `initial_ingress` |
| action_kind `deliver` | `initial_ingress` |
| action_kind `invoke` | `initial_ingress`, `tool_invocation`, `integration_interaction` |
| action_kind `transform` | `ai_system_action` |
| action_kind `persist` | `ai_system_action`, `tool_invocation` |
| action_kind `impact` | `impact` |
| executor_role `attacker` | `initial_ingress`, `external_precondition`, `impact`, `tool_invocation` |
| executor_role `system` | `ai_system_action`, `tool_invocation`, `integration_interaction`, `impact` |
| executor_role `operator` | `external_precondition`, `integration_interaction`, `impact` |

For every mapped leaf, its kind MUST be in the intersection of the
action-kind compatibility set and executor-role compatibility set.

#### Boundary, zone, and binding rules
- An `external_precondition` leaf MUST have no zone.
- An `external_precondition` leaf may map only an outside-boundary canonical
  step.  Inside-boundary and crossing-boundary external preconditions MUST
  remain unmapped with empty `projected_step_ids` and realizations.
- A mapped leaf MUST use the resource bindings from its canonical step; never
  substitute a binding from another step.
- Internal and crossing mapped steps MUST use the canonical compatible zone.

#### Technique identity rules
- Technique IDs are optional annotations, but when present they MUST use
  either an ATLAS format (`AML.T####` or `AML.T####.###`) or a LAAF format
  (`S#`, `M#`, or `L#`).  Do not invent or rewrite valid technique IDs.
